a different policy from its own indexical utility. Stepping back to a prior before knowing which role I occupy, the expected years come out to 2 for mutual pass, 2.5 for the mixed outcome, and 4 for mutual submit. So pass is the choice both copies reach from that shared vantage.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here, treating the two copies as the same function fed different inputs for Sasha and Rowan. Since the game is symmetric, I'm looking at which policy maps each role's input to an action, and I'm judging joint payoffs by the expected years for \"me\" averaged across both roles, since I don't yet know which I am. Under that averaging, (pass, pass) gives 2 years each, (submit, submit) gives 4, and the mixed (submit, pass) outcome gives either 0 or 5.\n\nI'm weighing whether the selfish argmax (submit for Sasha, pass for Rowan) is what P-FDT would pick, but that breaks down because each copy would then compute a different policy from its own indexical utility. Stepping back to a prior before knowing which role I occupy, the expected years come out to 2 for mutual pass, 2.5 for the mixed outcome, and 4 for mutual submit. So pass is the choice both copies reach from that shared vantage.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9081,"completion_tokens":946,"total_tokens":10027,"cost":0.055244,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055244,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036324,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01892},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":564,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}